	(text "D102 ORs USB VBUS against the carrier board's 5 V so the two\ncan be present at once without either back-feeding the other.\nOne BAT54C is two Schottkys; a shared cathode is exactly the\nOR. Cost of the diode drop: VSYS = 4.7 V, and the LDO needs\nonly 3.62 V to hold 3.3 V at 600 mA."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 25 250 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "672c8734-a81d-54d9-b057-0ac85b2cb3ac")
	)
	(text "SHEET 1 - INPUT, 5 V ORING, 3V3 AND THE BACKUP DOMAIN"
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 25 30 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a85976fb-c10e-5e08-8f73-f60f4051ff3f")
	)
	(text "D104 does the same job for the backup rail. V_BCKP holds the\nRTC and the ephemeris cache: keep it alive and the receiver\nhot-starts in ~1 s instead of cold-starting in ~30 s. With\nnothing on VBCKP_EXT it simply follows 3V3.\nC105/C106/C107 are the 4.7uF + 100nF + 33pF the LC29H\nhardware design asks for on this pin (section 3.2)."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 205 250 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f5e0faa5-a054-59ab-8d88-9ef4b8ba0355")
	)
